  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Bryant Lake is the Twin Cities' scenic technical test — a Timmy Gill design from 1999 that overlooks the lake through rolling hills and woods. From the standard pins it plays 5,557 feet at par 57, and every hole demands a real decision.",
    "It's pay to play through the Three Rivers Park District at $10 a round, with concrete tees and DISCatcher baskets. The lake views make the walk worth it even when the scores don't.",
    "One of the most-loved courses in Minnesota — bring your accuracy and your camera."
  ],
